11.85487 0 0 11.85487 130.69231 752.72978 Tm
(The conditions are boolean statements and the standard comparisons can b\e made. Valid )Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(comparisons include "<" \(less than\), ">" \(greater than\), "<=" \(less\ than or equal\), ">=" \(greater )Tj
T*
(than or equal\), "==" \(equal - this is two equal signs with no spaces b\etweeen them\), and "\230=" \(not )Tj
T*
(equal\). For example, the following code will set the variable j to be -\1: )Tj
/T1_1 1 Tf
0 -2.56195 TD
(a = 2;)Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(b = 3;)Tj
T*
(if \(a<b\) )Tj
T*
(    j = -1;)Tj
T*
(end     )Tj
/T1_0 1 Tf
0 -2.55232 TD
(Additional statements can be added for more refined decision making. The\ following code sets )Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(the variable j to be 2. )Tj
/T1_1 1 Tf
0 -2.56197 TD
(a = 4;)Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(b = 3;)Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(if \(a<b\) )Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(    j = -1;)Tj
T*
(else if \(a>b\))Tj
T*
(    j = 2;)Tj
T*
(end     )Tj
/T1_0 1 Tf
0 -2.55232 TD
(The )Tj
/T1_2 1 Tf
(else)Tj
/T1_0 1 Tf
( statement provides a catch all that will be executed if no other condit\ion is met. The )Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(following code sets the variable j to be 3. )Tj
/T1_1 1 Tf
0 -2.56197 TD
(a = 4;)Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(b = 4;)Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(if \(a<b\) )Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(    j = -1;)Tj
T*
(else if \(a>b\))Tj
T*
(    j = 2;)Tj
T*
(else )Tj
T*
(        j = 3)Tj
T*
(end     )Tj
/T1_0 1 Tf
