(This last example demonstrates one of the bad habits that Matlab allows \you to get away with. )Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(With finite precision arithmetic two variables are rarely exactly the sa\me. When using C or )Tj
T*
(FORTRAN you should never compare two floating numbers to see if they are\ the same. Instead )Tj
T*
(you should check to see if they are )Tj
/T1_3 1 Tf
(close)Tj
/T1_0 1 Tf
(. Matlab does not use integer arithmetic so if you check )Tj
T*
(to see if two numbers are the same it )Tj
/T1_3 1 Tf
(automatically)Tj
/T1_0 1 Tf
( checks to see if the variables are )Tj
/T1_2 1 Tf
(close)Tj
/T1_0 1 Tf
(. If you )Tj
T*
(were to use C or FORTRAN then that last example could get you into big t\rouble. but Matlab )Tj
T*
(does the checking for you in case the numbers are just really close. )Tj
0 -2.55714 TD
